  "artifact_text": "### Observations and Ruled-Out Leads\n\n**Observations:**\n1. Pod `orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556` fails its readiness probe with HTTP statuscode 503 (Kubernetes event).\n2. Pod `orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556` continuously logs database connection failure `[Errno -2] Name or service not known` (orders-api pod logs).\n3. Service `orders-db` exists in namespace `demo-apps`, but no service named `orders-db-primary` exists (v1 Service list).\n\n**Ruled-out leads:**\n1. Pod crashes or memory exhaustion were ruled out because the container has zero restarts and remains running (orders-api pod status).\n2. Database backend failure was ruled out because pod `orders-db-59f5787b7-jb5ww` is running and ready (orders-db pod status).\n\n### Root Cause\nDeployment CI-2459 updated `DB_HOST` in ConfigMap `orders-config` to non-existent hostname `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432` (deployment log CI-2459).\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe orders team should revert `DB_HOST` in ConfigMap `orders-config` back to `orders-db.demo-apps.svc:5432`.",
